{
    "background_story": "Isabela was a renowned fashion designer from a small town in Spain. Growing up, she was fascinated by the intricate details of traditional Spanish clothing, particularly the delicate organdy fabrics used in flamenco dresses. She spent years perfecting her craft, experimenting with organdy to create stunning, flowing garments that seemed to dance in the light. Isabela's big break came when a famous flamenco dancer wore one of her organdy creations on stage, mesmerizing the audience with its beauty and movement. Soon, Isabela's designs were in high demand, and she became known as the 'Organdy Queen' of Spanish fashion. Her boutique in Madrid attracted visitors from around the world, all seeking a taste of the elegance and drama that only Isabela's organdy masterpieces could provide.",
